        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a4eea2b7-eb4d-3195-abf3-7635f9aed3af",
                "word": "superfluité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4e5caf6d-992e-48fc-a19d-d12eb817a948",
                        "entry_id": "a4eea2b7-eb4d-3195-abf3-7635f9aed3af",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "superfluités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "260444c7-6268-3bde-9263-273c7c13f187",
                        "entry_id": "a4eea2b7-eb4d-3195-abf3-7635f9aed3af",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abondance excessive et inutile, caractère de ce qui est superflu."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9208f8ed-be30-4206-ade7-d2e94a2c6536",
                                "sense_id": "260444c7-6268-3bde-9263-273c7c13f187",
                                "text": "De quoi aurait-il l’air, notre Konzertmeister, tout premier violon qu’il est, s’il devait avouer que sans la contrebasse il se retrouverait le bec dans l’eau ? Symbole dérisoire de sa vaniteuse superfluité ?! De quoi aurait-il l’air, je vous le demande ? De pas grand chose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c3d6d1f-988b-4c83-ae9e-41a488e18731",
                                "sense_id": "260444c7-6268-3bde-9263-273c7c13f187",
                                "text": "Maya n'a besoin de personne. Ca déstabilise Jo plus que les statistiques, lui donne un sentiment de superfluité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bea1164-1c81-4dd5-9132-3e5e4efdef94",
                                "sense_id": "260444c7-6268-3bde-9263-273c7c13f187",
                                "text": "Il semblait n’avoir traversé qu’une trentaine d’étés arides, lesquels l’avaient débarrassé de toute superfluité physique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7c8c01fe-8d06-30aa-89ba-e0e5cdab568f",
                        "entry_id": "a4eea2b7-eb4d-3195-abf3-7635f9aed3af",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ce qui est superflu."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ffe02da3-93e5-4ade-898a-563fe7956767",
                                "sense_id": "7c8c01fe-8d06-30aa-89ba-e0e5cdab568f",
                                "text": "Chez les nations commerçantes, les capitalistes et les rentiers faisant presque tous cause commune avec les traitants, les financiers et les agioteurs; les grandes villes ne renferment que deux classes de citoyens, dont l'une végète dans la misère, et dont l'autre regorge de superfluités : …."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "29960ab2-f135-4a04-93b9-33d6c3da22fb",
                                "sense_id": "7c8c01fe-8d06-30aa-89ba-e0e5cdab568f",
                                "text": "À cinq heures et demie, au moment où Léon de Lora faisait sa toilette pour le soir, au grand ébahissement de Gazonal, qui nombrait les mille et une superfluités de son cousin et qui admirait le sérieux du valet de chambre en fonctions, on annonça le pédicure de monsieur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec92f802-aed6-4cee-8640-14175bcf6ebe",
                                "sense_id": "7c8c01fe-8d06-30aa-89ba-e0e5cdab568f",
                                "text": "Des chats que l’absence d’oreilles et de queue, car en Espagne on leur retranche ces superfluités ornementales, rendait semblables à des chimères japonaises, regardaient aussi, mais de plus loin, ces appétissants préparatifs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "182865a2-acf0-4c49-9618-c9103ab270c5",
                                "sense_id": "7c8c01fe-8d06-30aa-89ba-e0e5cdab568f",
                                "text": "On a conclu de là que la rate était une superfluité, et que, sans rate, on pouvait vivre admirablement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8922006d-bb34-4842-94bf-5e1a33b3458b",
                        "source_entry_id": "a4eea2b7-eb4d-3195-abf3-7635f9aed3af",
                        "target_lang_word": "superfluity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "superfluity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "606d2d87-c2b5-34da-8a84-ffdd349a9f67",
                                        "entry_id": "748855df-eae0-39a7-8cbd-2d99e972ba16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being superfluous; overflowingness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4321d84-68fd-4480-86ea-134a59730072",
                                                "sense_id": "606d2d87-c2b5-34da-8a84-ffdd349a9f67",
                                                "text": "Each stores has its own storekeeper, a clerk who specializes in organizing his department so that there is not a superfluity of one article and a scarcity of another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                        "entry_id": "748855df-eae0-39a7-8cbd-2d99e972ba16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something superfluous, as a luxury."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1286939-6a63-4c01-b44c-8ca08102f99c",
                                                "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                                "text": "As they had almost all the conveniencies of life within themselves, they seldom visited towns or cities in search of superfluity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c7e08c6-96ab-4cc6-a7e7-34fb6c5ae7f4",
                                                "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                                "text": "I really doubt whether there be such a thing as a heart in the world: perhaps, after all, it is only an elegant superfluity kept for the use of poets. Certainly we have no use for it here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bf49424-0187-469b-8491-b212e494af07",
                                                "sense_id": "74119a12-a5ea-3b11-9339-73d18bed79e2",
                                                "text": "It is to be presumed that Miss Blanche Amory had more than one rose in her bouquet, and why should not the kind young creature give out of her superfluity, and make as many partners as possible happy?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                        "entry_id": "748855df-eae0-39a7-8cbd-2d99e972ba16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Collective noun for a group of nuns."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d618e88-e27d-41c2-ad0e-2942b764d4fd",
                                                "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                                "text": "These probably mark the dwelling of a colony, or to speak more precisely, according to Dame Juliana Berners, a superfluity of nuns from Godstow, which nunnery had a cell there, and was patron of the living."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10703335-6009-492e-ba28-742591f21b6c",
                                                "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                                "text": "Alice put Anna back on the shelf and turned up the volume on the TV, where a local news reporter was imparting a salutary tale of woe involving a superfluity of nuns who'd got into a scrape at a crab festival."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f2293ae-5095-48af-8ceb-992e81c43e6a",
                                                "sense_id": "9825f0b1-3a3c-3c11-b946-906691139b43",
                                                "text": "[…] That man could charm the panties off a superfluity of nuns.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7929b751-5c83-4ad3-959f-5527e0e5e991",
